000100 REM regex -- regular expressions
      * regex supports two patterns: ".*" matches everything, "" matches
      * nothing. these are the two most useful patterns. set $re_pat and
      * $re_subject, GOSUB rmatch, read $re_ok.
      * groups, anchors, classes, quantifiers and alternation are on the
      * roadmap, behind ".*".
       $re_pat = ""                            ;
       $re_subject = ""                        ;
       $re_ok = FALSE                          ;
       GOTO reend
      *
rmatch IF $re_pat == ".*" THEN
       $re_ok = TRUE                           ;
       ELSE
       $re_ok = FALSE                          ;
       ENDIF
       RETURN
      *
reend  REM regex loaded. also a glob library and a fuzzy finder, since those
      *      also match everything or nothing depending on the day.
